From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:51:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kk: residency of sparse loads through texel buffer views

Metal has no sparse read of texture buffers, so sparse loads through texel
buffer views of sparse residency buffers reported every texel resident
(vkd3d-proton's CheckAccessFullyMapped after typed buffer loads:
test_buffer_feedback_instructions, test_sparse_default_mapping).

Sparse residency buffers get a residency texture: an R8Uint placement
sparse 2D array whose 64 KiB tiles are the buffer's pages, mapped to the
same heap pages by the same queue mapping updates. Texel buffer descriptors
grow to 32 bytes with the residency texture and the page lookup of the
view; sparse loads AND the residency of a sparse_read of their page's tile
into their code.

Metal crashes in updateTextureMappings when a texture mapping update
follows a buffer (or texture buffer) mapping update that followed a texture
mapping update with nothing in between; a signal of an event the queue
then waits for separates them (a signal alone let later buffer mapping
updates overtake earlier ones). Buffer binds go in passes (pages, views,
residency texture) so a submit needs at most one separator.
---
 src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c         |   8 +-
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_buffer_view.h       |   5 +
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_descriptor_set.c    |   4 +
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_descriptor_types.h  |  22 +-
 .../vulkan/kk_nir_lower_descriptors.c         |  81 ++++-
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_queue.h             |  18 +-
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_sparse.c            | 295 +++++++++++++++---
 7 files changed, 385 insertions(+), 48 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
index 6f8b662..cc99c3e 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
@@ -2609,9 +2609,11 @@ static bool
 msl_split_sparse_fetch(nir_builder *b, nir_instr *instr, void *data)
 {
    nir_def *def;
-   /* Multisampled and buffer images are never sparse (no sparseResidency*
-    * samples features, Vulkan has no sparse texel buffers): their texels are
-    * all resident and MSL has no sparse read for them. */
+   /* Multisampled images are never sparse (no sparseResidency*Samples
+    * features) and MSL has no sparse read of texture buffers: these reads
+    * are resident here. Texel buffers of sparse buffers get the residency of
+    * their page from the driver (kk_nir_lower_descriptors.c), ANDed into the
+    * code. */
    bool always_resident;
    if (instr->type == nir_instr_type_tex && nir_instr_as_tex(instr)->is_sparse) {
       nir_tex_instr *tex = nir_instr_as_tex(instr);
